# Somnia Shannon testnet (chain 50312). THROWAWAY KEYS ONLY.
PRIVATE_KEY=0x
INDEXER_URL=https://dev.smk.somnia.host/v1/graphql
WS_RPC_URL=wss://api.infra.testnet.somnia.network/ws

# Postgres. Production is RAILWAY Postgres, in the same project and region as
# the executor (moved off Supabase on 16 sep — the free plan allows two active
# projects, a third was created, and the game's database got paused out from
# under it). On Railway the executor uses the private URL and needs no pooler
# at all:
#
#   DATABASE_URL="${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}"   <- private, service-to-service
#
# and Vercel uses the same database through the service's TCP proxy (Railway →
# Postgres → Variables → PUBLIC_DATABASE_URL).
#
# The pooler notes below are Supabase-specific and kept because the lesson
# generalises to any pgbouncer in front of Prisma:
#
#   5432  session mode      <- the EXECUTOR and local dev. One long-lived
#                              connection, prepared statements intact.
#   6543  transaction mode  <- serverless only (Vercel), with ?pgbouncer=true.
#
# Running the executor through 6543 costs FOUR protocol round trips per query
# instead of one (Prisma has to DEALLOCATE around every statement). Measured on
# a normal home connection: 10 reads took 30.4s through 6543 and 6.7s through
# 5432, and a single tick ballooned to 52 round trips and ~54s — long enough
# that the game visibly stalled between rounds.
# connection_limit matters on the SESSION pooler: it allows 15 clients total and
# Prisma opens ~9 per process by default, so a dev server plus the executor
# exhaust it and the executor starts failing with EMAXCONNSESSION. The
# executor is sequential; 4 is plenty.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DBNAME"
# Migrations / prisma db push. Same URL is fine on Railway (no pooler in the
# path); on Supabase this had to be the direct connection, not the pooler.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DBNAME"

# ArenaRegistry — leave unset and the game runs identically without the
# on-chain mirror.
REGISTRY=
# The reactivity subscription that lets the chain settle rounds itself. Written
# by `npx tsx scripts/resubscribe.ts --send`. It DIES if the house wallet drops
# under 32 STT and must be re-created — see AGENTS.md.
REACTIVITY_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=
